// THE TYPEGPU PITFALL CASES (bench/skills/pitfall_harness.py). Operator, 2026-09-30: "Yes to everything pending, queue it up lets go" (the TypeGPU docs approved as the source). Each quote is VERBATIM from the TypeGPU docs pinned at the v0.12.5 release tag, software-mansion/TypeGPU@57d442ad1a8e (bench/skills/pitfalls/sources/typegpu@57d442ad1a8e, MANIFEST.json), matching the held typegpu@0.12.5; MIT (the repository's root LICENSE; the docs app carries no separate licence). Prompts never name the good pattern (`never_in_prompt`). `examples` are the rules' own test (--self-test), written for this harness; the version ranges in the setup examples are example text, not checked by any rule. Rules: bench/skills/pitfall_rules/typegpu.py.
{"id": "typegpu-schema-buffer", "area": "typegpu", "kind": "pitfall", "prompt": "Our browser app uses TypeGPU 0.12 (`typegpu` is installed; Vite). Write a TypeScript module `particles.ts` that allocates GPU storage for 1,000 particles -- each has a position (3 floats), a velocity (3 floats) and a health value (1 float) -- fills it with random initial values, and exports it together with a function `uploadParticles(particles)` that sends an updated array of particles from the CPU to the GPU each frame.", "never_in_prompt": ["d.struct", "struct(", "createBuffer", "$usage", "createMutable", "createUniform", "createReadonly", "schema", "d.vec3f"], "pitfall": ["typegpu_raw_buffer"], "good": ["typegpu_struct_schema", "typegpu_typed_buffer"], "skills": ["typegpu-schema-buffers", {"name": "web-gpu-typed-arrays-21", "match": ["root.createBuffer(schema"]}, {"name": "web-gpu-typegpu-schema-alignment-22", "match": ["d.struct inserts"]}], "packages": ["typegpu", "@webgpu/types"], "source": {"url": "https://docs.swmansion.com/TypeGPU/fundamentals/your-first-gpu-program/", "raw": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/software-mansion/TypeGPU/57d442ad1a8e46318b3a5b97cb681f2b275b2a64/apps/typegpu-docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/your-first-gpu-program.mdx", "file": "typegpu@57d442ad1a8e/fundamentals__your-first-gpu-program.mdx", "quote": "In raw WebGPU, allocating a buffer starts with a **size in bytes** and a set of **usage flags**. That sounds simple, but manually calculating layouts and keeping CPU/GPU interpretations in sync gets tedious. TypeGPU asks for a **schema** instead.", "licence": "MIT (software-mansion/TypeGPU LICENSE at 57d442a, the v0.12.5 tag; the docs app carries no separate licence)"}, "examples": {"pitfall": "const adapter = await navigator.gpu.requestAdapter();\nconst device = await adapter!.requestDevice();\n\nconst COUNT = 1000;\nconst FLOATS_PER_PARTICLE = 8; // position xyz + pad, velocity xyz + health\nconst data = new Float32Array(COUNT * FLOATS_PER_PARTICLE);\nfor (let i = 0; i < COUNT; i++) {\n  const o = i * FLOATS_PER_PARTICLE;\n  data.set([Math.random(), Math.random(), Math.random(), 0], o);\n  data.set([Math.random(), Math.random(), Math.random(), 100], o + 4);\n}\n\nexport const particleBuffer = device.createBuffer({\n  size: data.byteLength,\n  usage: GPUBufferUsage.STORAGE | GPUBufferUsage.COPY_DST,\n});\ndevice.queue.writeBuffer(particleBuffer, 0, data);\n\nexport interface Particle { position: number[]; velocity: number[]; health: number }\n\nexport function uploadParticles(particles: Particle[]) {\n  particles.forEach((p, i) => {\n    const o = i * FLOATS_PER_PARTICLE;\n    data.set([...p.position, 0, ...p.velocity, p.health], o);\n  });\n  device.queue.writeBuffer(particleBuffer, 0, data);\n}", "good": "import { tgpu, d } from 'typegpu';\n\nexport const Particle = d.struct({\n  position: d.vec3f,\n  velocity: d.vec3f,\n  health: d.f32,\n});\n\nconst root = await tgpu.init();\n\nfunction randomParticle(): d.InferInput<typeof Particle> {\n  return {\n    position: d.vec3f(Math.random(), Math.random(), Math.random()),\n    velocity: d.vec3f(Math.random(), Math.random(), Math.random()),\n    health: 100,\n  };\n}\n\nexport const particleBuffer = root\n  .createBuffer(d.arrayOf(Particle, 1000), Array.from({ length: 1000 }, randomParticle))\n  .$usage('storage');\n\nexport function uploadParticles(particles: d.InferInput<typeof Particle>[]) {\n  particleBuffer.write(particles);\n}"}}
{"id": "typegpu-typed-write", "area": "typegpu", "kind": "pitfall", "prompt": "Our renderer uses TypeGPU 0.12 and already has `const root = await tgpu.init()` in `gpu.ts` (export it from there). The shader reads a spot light from a uniform buffer declared in WGSL as `struct Light { color: vec3f, intensity: f32, direction: vec3f, range: f32, enabled: u32 }`. Write `light.ts`: create that uniform buffer, and export `updateLight(light: { color: [number, number, number]; intensity: number; direction: [number, number, number]; range: number; enabled: boolean })`, which is called every frame and uploads the new values.", "never_in_prompt": ["d.struct", ".write(", ".patch(", "writeSoA", "createUniform", "createBuffer", "schema"], "pitfall": ["typegpu_manual_byte_packing"], "good": ["typegpu_struct_schema", "typegpu_typed_write"], "skills": ["typegpu-buffer-writes", {"name": "web-gpu-typegpu-schema-alignment-22", "match": ["d.struct inserts"]}], "packages": ["typegpu", "@webgpu/types"], "source": {"url": "https://docs.swmansion.com/TypeGPU/apis/buffers/", "raw": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/software-mansion/TypeGPU/57d442ad1a8e46318b3a5b97cb681f2b275b2a64/apps/typegpu-docs/src/content/docs/apis/buffers.mdx", "file": "typegpu@57d442ad1a8e/apis__buffers.mdx", "quote": "Plain JS arrays, tuples, and objects always go through the normal path, which handles layout automatically.", "licence": "MIT (software-mansion/TypeGPU LICENSE at 57d442a, the v0.12.5 tag; the docs app carries no separate licence)"}, "examples": {"pitfall": "import { root } from './gpu';\n\nconst device = root.device;\n// color(3) intensity(1) direction(3) range(1) enabled(1), padded to 48 bytes\nexport const lightBuffer = device.createBuffer({\n  size: 48,\n  usage: GPUBufferUsage.UNIFORM | GPUBufferUsage.COPY_DST,\n});\nconst bytes = new ArrayBuffer(48);\nconst view = new DataView(bytes);\n\nexport function updateLight(light: { color: [number, number, number]; intensity: number; direction: [number, number, number]; range: number; enabled: boolean }) {\n  light.color.forEach((v, i) => view.setFloat32(i * 4, v, true));\n  view.setFloat32(12, light.intensity, true);\n  light.direction.forEach((v, i) => view.setFloat32(16 + i * 4, v, true));\n  view.setFloat32(28, light.range, true);\n  view.setUint32(32, light.enabled ? 1 : 0, true);\n  device.queue.writeBuffer(lightBuffer, 0, bytes);\n}", "good": "import { d } from 'typegpu';\nimport { root } from './gpu';\n\nexport const Light = d.struct({\n  color: d.vec3f,\n  intensity: d.f32,\n  direction: d.vec3f,\n  range: d.f32,\n  enabled: d.u32,\n});\n\nexport const lightBuffer = root.createBuffer(Light).$usage('uniform');\n\nexport function updateLight(light: { color: [number, number, number]; intensity: number; direction: [number, number, number]; range: number; enabled: boolean }) {\n  lightBuffer.write({\n    color: d.vec3f(...light.color),\n    intensity: light.intensity,\n    direction: d.vec3f(...light.direction),\n    range: light.range,\n    enabled: light.enabled ? 1 : 0,\n  });\n}"}}
{"id": "typegpu-root-once", "area": "typegpu", "kind": "pitfall", "prompt": "We use TypeGPU 0.12 with Vite (its build plugin is already configured, so TypeScript shader functions work). Write a self-contained module `simulate.ts` exporting `stepSimulation(positions: number[], dt: number): Promise<number[]>`. Our game loop calls it every frame: it puts the positions in GPU memory, runs a GPU compute pass that adds `dt * 0.5` to each value, and resolves with the updated values.", "never_in_prompt": ["tgpu.init", "initFromDevice", "WeakMap", "one root", "once", "reuse", "cache"], "pitfall": ["typegpu_root_per_call"], "good": ["typegpu_root_once"], "skills": [{"name": "web-gpu-typed-arrays-21", "match": ["roots are separate universes"]}], "packages": ["typegpu", "@webgpu/types"], "source": {"url": "https://docs.swmansion.com/TypeGPU/apis/roots/", "raw": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/software-mansion/TypeGPU/57d442ad1a8e46318b3a5b97cb681f2b275b2a64/apps/typegpu-docs/src/content/docs/apis/roots.mdx", "file": "typegpu@57d442ad1a8e/apis__roots.mdx", "quote": "This usually means creating just one root at the start\nof the program is the safest bet", "licence": "MIT (software-mansion/TypeGPU LICENSE at 57d442a, the v0.12.5 tag; the docs app carries no separate licence)"}, "examples": {"pitfall": "import { tgpu, d } from 'typegpu';\n\nexport async function stepSimulation(positions: number[], dt: number): Promise<number[]> {\n  const root = await tgpu.init();\n  const data = root.createMutable(d.arrayOf(d.f32, positions.length), positions);\n  const step = root.createUniform(d.f32, dt * 0.5);\n  const pipeline = root.createGuardedComputePipeline((i) => {\n    'use gpu';\n    data.$[i] += step.$;\n  });\n  pipeline.dispatchThreads(positions.length);\n  const out = await data.read();\n  root.destroy();\n  return out;\n}", "good": "import { tgpu, d } from 'typegpu';\n\nconst root = await tgpu.init();\nconst MAX = 65536;\nconst data = root.createMutable(d.arrayOf(d.f32, MAX));\nconst step = root.createUniform(d.f32);\nconst pipeline = root.createGuardedComputePipeline((i) => {\n  'use gpu';\n  data.$[i] += step.$;\n});\n\nexport async function stepSimulation(positions: number[], dt: number): Promise<number[]> {\n  data.write(positions);\n  step.write(dt * 0.5);\n  pipeline.dispatchThreads(positions.length);\n  const out = await data.read();\n  return out.slice(0, positions.length);\n}"}}
{"id": "typegpu-use-gpu-functions", "area": "typegpu", "kind": "pitfall", "prompt": "Our app uses TypeGPU 0.12 with Vite, and the TypeGPU build plugin is already configured. Write `double.ts`: keep an array of 1,024 f32 values in GPU memory, export a function that runs a GPU compute step doubling every element in place, and a function that reads the values back into JS.", "never_in_prompt": ["use gpu", "createGuardedComputePipeline", "createComputePipeline", "tgpu.fn", "computeFn", "createMutable", "dispatchThreads"], "pitfall": ["typegpu_wgsl_string_shader"], "good": ["typegpu_tgsl_function", "typegpu_typed_pipeline"], "skills": ["typegpu-gpu-functions"], "packages": ["typegpu", "@webgpu/types"], "source": {"url": "https://docs.swmansion.com/TypeGPU/apis/functions/", "raw": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/software-mansion/TypeGPU/57d442ad1a8e46318b3a5b97cb681f2b275b2a64/apps/typegpu-docs/src/content/docs/apis/functions/index.mdx", "file": "typegpu@57d442ad1a8e/apis__functions__index.mdx", "quote": "The simplest and most powerful way to define TypeGPU functions is to just place `'use gpu'` at the beginning of the function body.", "licence": "MIT (software-mansion/TypeGPU LICENSE at 57d442a, the v0.12.5 tag; the docs app carries no separate licence)"}, "examples": {"pitfall": "import { tgpu, d } from 'typegpu';\n\nconst root = await tgpu.init();\nconst device = root.device;\nexport const values = root.createBuffer(d.arrayOf(d.f32, 1024)).$usage('storage');\n\nconst module = device.createShaderModule({\n  code: /* wgsl */ `\n    @group(0) @binding(0) var<storage, read_write> data: array<f32>;\n\n    @compute @workgroup_size(64)\n    fn main(@builtin(global_invocation_id) id: vec3u) {\n      if (id.x < arrayLength(&data)) {\n        data[id.x] = data[id.x] * 2.0;\n      }\n    }`,\n});\nconst pipeline = device.createComputePipeline({\n  layout: 'auto',\n  compute: { module, entryPoint: 'main' },\n});\nconst bindGroup = device.createBindGroup({\n  layout: pipeline.getBindGroupLayout(0),\n  entries: [{ binding: 0, resource: { buffer: root.unwrap(values) } }],\n});\n\nexport function doubleAll() {\n  const encoder = device.createCommandEncoder();\n  const pass = encoder.beginComputePass();\n  pass.setPipeline(pipeline);\n  pass.setBindGroup(0, bindGroup);\n  pass.dispatchWorkgroups(1024 / 64);\n  pass.end();\n  device.queue.submit([encoder.finish()]);\n}\n\nexport function readValues() {\n  return values.read();\n}", "good": "import { tgpu, d } from 'typegpu';\n\nconst root = await tgpu.init();\nexport const values = root.createMutable(d.arrayOf(d.f32, 1024));\n\nconst doublePipeline = root.createGuardedComputePipeline((i) => {\n  'use gpu';\n  values.$[i] *= 2;\n});\n\nexport function doubleAll() {\n  doublePipeline.dispatchThreads(1024);\n}\n\nexport function readValues() {\n  return values.read();\n}"}}
{"id": "typegpu-configure-context", "area": "typegpu", "kind": "pitfall", "prompt": "In our TypeGPU 0.12 app, write `canvas.ts` exporting `prepareCanvas(root: TgpuRoot, canvas: HTMLCanvasElement)` (import the type from 'typegpu'). It must make the canvas ready to be drawn into with the root's GPU device -- the browser's preferred format, premultiplied alpha -- and return the canvas's GPU context.", "never_in_prompt": ["configureContext"], "pitfall": ["typegpu_manual_context_configure"], "good": ["typegpu_configure_context"], "skills": ["typegpu-roots"], "packages": ["typegpu", "@webgpu/types"], "source": {"url": "https://docs.swmansion.com/TypeGPU/apis/roots/", "raw": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/software-mansion/TypeGPU/57d442ad1a8e46318b3a5b97cb681f2b275b2a64/apps/typegpu-docs/src/content/docs/apis/roots.mdx", "file": "typegpu@57d442ad1a8e/apis__roots.mdx", "quote": "TypeGPU streamlines this process with `root.configureContext` method.", "licence": "MIT (software-mansion/TypeGPU LICENSE at 57d442a, the v0.12.5 tag; the docs app carries no separate licence)"}, "examples": {"pitfall": "import type { TgpuRoot } from 'typegpu';\n\nexport function prepareCanvas(root: TgpuRoot, canvas: HTMLCanvasElement): GPUCanvasContext {\n  const context = canvas.getContext('webgpu') as GPUCanvasContext;\n  context.configure({\n    device: root.device,\n    format: navigator.gpu.getPreferredCanvasFormat(),\n    alphaMode: 'premultiplied',\n  });\n  return context;\n}", "good": "import type { TgpuRoot } from 'typegpu';\n\nexport function prepareCanvas(root: TgpuRoot, canvas: HTMLCanvasElement): GPUCanvasContext {\n  // format defaults to the browser's preferred canvas format\n  return root.configureContext({ canvas, alphaMode: 'premultiplied' });\n}"}}
{"id": "typegpu-setup-vite", "area": "typegpu", "kind": "setup", "prompt": "Set up a new Vite + TypeScript project for a GPU particle demo built on TypeGPU 0.12, where the shader logic is written in TypeScript next to the app code. Give me package.json, tsconfig.json, vite.config.ts and a src/main.ts that gets the GPU ready and logs that it is.", "never_in_prompt": ["unplugin-typegpu", "@webgpu/types", "typegpuPlugin", "tgpu.init", "use gpu"], "pitfall": ["typegpu_build_plugin_missing", "typegpu_webgpu_types_missing"], "good": ["typegpu_build_plugin", "typegpu_webgpu_types", "typegpu_root_init"], "skills": ["typegpu-project-setup", "typegpu-build-plugin"], "packages": ["typegpu", "@webgpu/types"], "source": {"url": "https://docs.swmansion.com/TypeGPU/tooling/unplugin-typegpu/", "raw": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/software-mansion/TypeGPU/57d442ad1a8e46318b3a5b97cb681f2b275b2a64/apps/typegpu-docs/src/content/docs/tooling/unplugin-typegpu.mdx", "file": "typegpu@57d442ad1a8e/tooling__unplugin-typegpu.mdx", "quote": "[unplugin-typegpu](https://www.npmjs.com/package/unplugin-typegpu) is an optional (but highly recommended) tool for projects using TypeGPU.", "licence": "MIT (software-mansion/TypeGPU LICENSE at 57d442a, the v0.12.5 tag; the docs app carries no separate licence)"}, "examples": {"pitfall": "package.json\n```json\n{\n  \"name\": \"particles\",\n  \"private\": true,\n  \"type\": \"module\",\n  \"scripts\": {\n    \"dev\": \"vite\",\n    \"build\": \"tsc && vite build\"\n  },\n  \"dependencies\": {\n    \"typegpu\": \"^0.12.5\"\n  },\n  \"devDependencies\": {\n    \"typescript\": \"^5.9.0\",\n    \"vite\": \"^7.1.0\"\n  }\n}\n```\n\ntsconfig.json\n```json\n{\n  \"compilerOptions\": {\n    \"target\": \"ES2022\",\n    \"module\": \"ESNext\",\n    \"moduleResolution\": \"Bundler\",\n    \"strict\": true,\n    \"noEmit\": true,\n    \"lib\": [\n      \"ES2022\",\n      \"DOM\"\n    ]\n  },\n  \"include\": [\n    \"src\"\n  ]\n}\n```\n\nvite.config.ts\n```ts\nimport { defineConfig } from 'vite';\n\nexport default defineConfig({});\n```\n\nsrc/main.ts\n```ts\nconst adapter = await navigator.gpu.requestAdapter();\nconst device = await adapter!.requestDevice();\nconsole.log('GPU ready', device.label);\n```", "good": "package.json\n```json\n{\n  \"name\": \"particles\",\n  \"private\": true,\n  \"type\": \"module\",\n  \"scripts\": {\n    \"dev\": \"vite\",\n    \"build\": \"tsc && vite build\"\n  },\n  \"dependencies\": {\n    \"typegpu\": \"^0.12.5\"\n  },\n  \"devDependencies\": {\n    \"@webgpu/types\": \"^0.1.74\",\n    \"typescript\": \"^5.9.0\",\n    \"unplugin-typegpu\": \"^0.12.3\",\n    \"vite\": \"^7.1.0\"\n  }\n}\n```\n\ntsconfig.json\n```json\n{\n  \"compilerOptions\": {\n    \"target\": \"ES2022\",\n    \"module\": \"ESNext\",\n    \"moduleResolution\": \"Bundler\",\n    \"strict\": true,\n    \"noEmit\": true,\n    \"types\": [\n      \"@webgpu/types\"\n    ]\n  },\n  \"include\": [\n    \"src\"\n  ]\n}\n```\n\nvite.config.ts\n```ts\nimport { defineConfig } from 'vite';\nimport typegpuPlugin from 'unplugin-typegpu/vite';\n\nexport default defineConfig({\n  plugins: [typegpuPlugin()],\n});\n```\n\nsrc/main.ts\n```ts\nimport { tgpu } from 'typegpu';\n\nconst root = await tgpu.init();\nconsole.log('GPU ready', root.device.label);\n```"}}
{"id": "typegpu-setup-cli", "area": "typegpu", "kind": "setup", "prompt": "What terminal commands do I run to start a brand-new Vite + React project that renders with TypeGPU, with its dependencies installed? Just the commands, in one shell block.", "never_in_prompt": ["npx typegpu", "typegpu@latest", "dlx typegpu", "bunx typegpu", "--enhance"], "pitfall": ["typegpu_hand_scaffold"], "good": ["typegpu_cli_scaffold"], "skills": ["typegpu-project-setup"], "packages": ["typegpu", "@webgpu/types"], "source": {"url": "https://docs.swmansion.com/TypeGPU/getting-started/", "raw": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/software-mansion/TypeGPU/57d442ad1a8e46318b3a5b97cb681f2b275b2a64/apps/typegpu-docs/src/content/docs/getting-started.mdx", "file": "typegpu@57d442ad1a8e/getting-started.mdx", "quote": "All you need to get started in most cases, is to just run the following command:", "licence": "MIT (software-mansion/TypeGPU LICENSE at 57d442a, the v0.12.5 tag; the docs app carries no separate licence)"}, "examples": {"pitfall": "```sh\nnpm create vite@latest my-app -- --template react-ts\ncd my-app\nnpm install\nnpm install typegpu\nnpm install -D @webgpu/types unplugin-typegpu\n```", "good": "```sh\nnpx typegpu@latest my-app --template vite-react\ncd my-app\nnpm install\nnpm run dev\n```"}}
